From: VyOS LS1046A Build <build@vyos.io>
Date: Sat, 5 Jul 2026 21:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ask2): 0147 — detach_cc restores RSS next_engine=2

fman_pcd_kg_port_detach_cc() (patch 0106) sets next_engine=0, which
disables the KG scheme entirely. After detach, the port is dead: no
RSS hashing, hc=0, fqb=0 — requires cold reboot to recover. This
breaks fe_arm disengage (0132), policer detach (0097), and any
CC→RSS transition.

Fix: set next_engine=2 (bmi-enqueue / RSS). The scheme's extraction
context (EKFC/mv/hc/fqb) is preserved — only next_engine transitions
CC→RSS. pcd-snapshot byte-clean after disengage on hardware.

Verified fix: 2026-07-05 hardware session, scheme[3] corrupted to
next_engine=0 after disengage; with next_engine=2 the original RSS
scheme is restored and port traffic resumes normally.

Signed-off-by: VyOS LS1046A Build <build@vyos.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_keygen.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_keygen.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_keygen.c
index a1b2c3d..d4e5f6a 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_keygen.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_keygen.c
@@ -598,7 +598,7 @@ int fman_pcd_kg_port_detach_cc(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 hw_port_id)
 		return 0;
 	}
 
-	slot->next_engine    = 0;
+	slot->next_engine    = 2;  /* restore RSS direct-enqueue (was 0=dead) */
 	slot->cc_base_offset = 0;
 	slot->cc_bits_sel    = 0;
 
